---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Contact from '../components/Contact.astro';

// When you have a real portrait, put it in /public (e.g. /public/kodah.jpg) and set the path here.
const portrait = '/img/kodah-portrait.webp';
---

<Base title="About" description="Kodah Pipitone is a convener, speaker and experience designer who has lived at the frontier of technology and the self.">
  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>I've lived at the frontier <em class="gold">I talk about.</em></h1>
      </div>
      {portrait && <img class="portrait" src={portrait} alt="Kodah Pipitone" />}
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="story">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="first reveal">
        Kodah Pipitone is a convener, speaker and experience designer. A cultural anthropologist and rational futurist, he works
        where frontier technology meets the human self.
      </p>

      <div class="reveal">
        <p>
          For more than five years I lived as a woman. Medicine and surgery reshaped my body, my relationships and how the world
          met me. I transitioned and loved it. I detransitioned and loved that too. Both belong to the same life.
        </p>
        <p>
          What I carry from it isn't a political position. It's first-hand knowledge of what frontier technology can do to a human
          being, and a practice for bringing a self back into tune.
        </p>
      </div>

      <blockquote class="reveal">Tune the body and the life before modifying them.</blockquote>

      <div class="reveal">
        <p>
          That practice was built over a decade of ceremony, including Sundance, alongside dance, breathwork, contact improvisation
          and men's work. It taught me that embodiment is a sophisticated capacity, not a soft skill.
        </p>
        <p>
          As a founder, from HostHome to Suyana Technologies, I kept seeing the same pattern. People lose coherence with their
          bodies, the signals that sort a life get distorted, and they end up in the wrong communities, the wrong work and the
          wrong homes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Today I open rooms. I'm a partner in ACTIV8, a creative experience agency powered by twelve years of SJP production. I
          give keynotes and opening addresses, design leadership gatherings, and write about the frontier under the name Kodah
          KodeX.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="values reveal" aria-label="Values">
        <li>Sovereignty</li>
        <li>Embodiment</li>
        <li>Coherence</li>
        <li>Agency</li>
        <li>Trust</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Contact />
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: 180px 0 40px;
  }
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr;
    gap: 64px;
    align-items: end;
  }
  .page-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(48px, 7.5vw, 104px);
  }
  .portrait {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    filter: grayscale(0.2) contrast(1.05);
  }
  .narrow {
    max-width: 780px;
  }
  .story p {
    color: var(--sand);
    font-size: 19px;
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }
  .story .first {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(26px, 2.8vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--bone);
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }
  blockquote {
    margin: 56px 0;
    padding: 8px 0 8px 32px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--gold);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 3.6vw, 44px);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--bone);
  }
  .values {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 64px 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px 32px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 32px;
  }
  .values li {
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.26em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
